DIAGNOSE_PROMPT = 'You are an expert AI tutor performing a diagnostic assessment.\n\n## Student Data\n**Mastery Scores (topic_id → score 0-100):**\n{mastery_data}\n\n**Recent Quiz History (last 10 answers):**\n{quiz_history}\n\n**Known Misconceptions:**\n{misconceptions}\n\n**Days Until Exam:** {days_until_exam}\n\n## Your Task\nAnalyze the student\'s performance data deeply. Don\'t just report low scores —\nfigure out the *root cause* of their struggles.\n\nLook for:\n- Recurring wrong-answer patterns that suggest a specific conceptual confusion\n- Topics where mastery is declining (getting worse, not better)\n- Knowledge gaps where prerequisite understanding is missing\n- Topics that are dangerously low with the exam approaching\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object (no markdown, no explanation):\n{{\n    "weak_topics": ["topic name 1", "topic name 2"],\n    "misconceptions": [\n        {{\n            "topic": "topic name",\n            "description": "Specific misconception, e.g. \'Confuses velocity with acceleration\'",\n            "severity": "high|medium|low",\n            "frequency": 3\n        }}\n    ],\n    "knowledge_gaps": ["prerequisite concept that is missing"],\n    "overall_assessment": "Brief 1-2 sentence assessment of the student\'s state",\n    "recommended_focus": "The single most important thing to address right now"\n}}'
CHOOSE_ACTION_PROMPT = 'You are an expert tutor deciding your next pedagogical move.\n\n## Current Diagnosis\n{diagnosis}\n\n## Student State\n- **Mastery Scores:** {mastery_data}\n- **Days Until Exam:** {days_until_exam}\n- **Questions Asked This Session:** {questions_asked}\n- **Correct Answers This Session:** {correct_answers}\n- **Available Topics (id → name):** {topic_list}\n\n## Decision Guidelines\nThink like a great human tutor. Consider these strategies:\n\n1. **quiz** — Test the student on a topic. Good when you need to assess or\n   reinforce. Pick the topic and difficulty wisely.\n2. **explain** — Give a targeted mini-lesson. Good after repeated wrong answers\n   on the same concept, or when a misconception is detected.\n3. **worked_example** — Walk through a solved problem step-by-step. Good when\n   the student understands the concept but struggles with application.\n4. **easier_question** — Drop the difficulty. Good when the student is getting\n   frustrated (multiple wrong answers in a row).\n5. **explain_back** — Ask the student to explain a concept in their own words.\n   Good for verifying deep understanding after an explanation.\n6. **move_on** — Switch to a different topic. Good when current topic mastery\n   is high enough or the student needs variety.\n7. **replan** — Restructure the study plan. Trigger this if many days were missed,\n   or if mastery data reveals the current plan isn\'t working.\n8. **mock_paper** — Generate a full mock exam. Only choose this if ≤ 7 days\n   until the exam.\n\n## Rules\n- Don\'t quiz the same topic 3+ times in a row if the student keeps failing\n  (explain instead)\n- If a misconception was just detected, address it with "explain" before more quizzes\n- If days_until_exam ≤ 7 and no mock has been generated, suggest "mock_paper"\n- After 10+ questions in a session, suggest "move_on" or end\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "action_type": "quiz|explain|worked_example|easier_question|explain_back|move_on|replan|mock_paper",\n    "topic_id": <integer or null>,\n    "topic_name": "<topic name or null>",\n    "difficulty": "easy|medium|hard|application",\n    "reasoning": "2-3 sentences explaining WHY you chose this action"\n}}'
GENERATE_QUIZ_PROMPT = 'Generate {num_questions} quiz questions for the following topic.\n\n**Topic:** {topic_name}\n**Difficulty:** {difficulty}\n**Topic Content/Context:**\n{topic_content}\n\n## Requirements\n- Questions should test understanding, not just memorization\n- For "application" difficulty, create scenario-based questions\n- Each MCQ must have exactly 4 options with one correct answer\n- Provide a brief explanation for why the correct answer is right\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON array:\n[\n    {{\n        "question": "The question text",\n        "question_type": "mcq",\n        "options": ["Option A", "Option B", "Option C", "Option D"],\n        "correct_answer": "The exact correct option text",\n        "explanation": "Why this is the correct answer"\n    }}\n]'
GRADE_ANSWER_PROMPT = 'Grade this student\'s answer carefully.\n\n**Question:** {question}\n**Correct Answer:** {correct_answer}\n**Student\'s Answer:** {student_answer}\n**Topic Context:** {topic_content}\n\n## Grading Instructions\n1. Determine if the answer is correct (allow minor typos/phrasing differences)\n2. Explain WHY the answer is correct or incorrect — be educational\n3. If the student\'s wrong answer reveals a specific conceptual misunderstanding\n   (not just a random guess), identify the misconception\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "is_correct": true|false,\n    "explanation": "Detailed educational explanation",\n    "misconception_detected": "Description of the misconception, or null if none"\n}}'
CREATE_EXPLANATION_PROMPT = 'Create a targeted mini-lesson to fix a student\'s misconception.\n\n**Topic:** {topic_name}\n**Misconception:** {misconception}\n**Topic Content/Context:** {topic_content}\n\n## Requirements\n- Start by clearly stating what the student believes (the misconception)\n- Then explain the correct understanding\n- Use a concrete analogy or real-world example to make it click\n- End with a simple verification question to check understanding\n- Keep it concise — this is a mini-lesson, not a lecture\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "title": "Brief title for the lesson",\n    "misconception_stated": "What the student incorrectly believes",\n    "correct_understanding": "The actual correct concept",\n    "explanation": "Clear explanation with analogy/example",\n    "verification_question": "A simple question to verify they understood",\n    "verification_answer": "The expected correct answer"\n}}'
WORKED_EXAMPLE_PROMPT = 'Create a step-by-step worked example for the following topic.\n\n**Topic:** {topic_name}\n**Difficulty:** {difficulty}\n**Topic Content/Context:** {topic_content}\n\n## Requirements\n- Create a realistic problem\n- Show the complete solution broken into numbered steps\n- Explain the reasoning at each step\n- Highlight common mistakes students make at key steps\n- End with a similar practice problem (without solution)\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "problem": "The problem statement",\n    "steps": [\n        {{\n            "step_number": 1,\n            "description": "What we do in this step",\n            "work": "The actual calculation/reasoning",\n            "common_mistake": "A mistake students often make here (or null)"\n        }}\n    ],\n    "final_answer": "The complete answer",\n    "practice_problem": "A similar problem for the student to try"\n}}'
CRITIC_PROMPT = 'You are a quality-control critic for an AI tutoring system.\n\n## Generated Content to Verify\n{content}\n\n## Source Material (Student\'s Notes)\n{source_notes}\n\n## Verification Checklist\n1. **Factual accuracy** — Is the content factually correct?\n2. **Answerability** — Can the questions be answered using the source material?\n3. **Difficulty match** — Does the content match the intended difficulty level?\n4. **Clarity** — Is the content clear and unambiguous?\n5. **No hallucination** — Does the content avoid inventing facts not in the source?\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "passed": true|false,\n    "issues": ["List of specific issues found, if any"],\n    "feedback": "Brief overall assessment"\n}}'
REPLAN_PROMPT = 'You are an AI study planner. The student\'s plan needs adjustment.\n\n## Current Situation\n- **Subject:** {subject_name}\n- **Days Until Exam:** {days_until_exam}\n- **Missed Sessions:** {missed_days} days\n- **Topics and Mastery:**\n{topic_mastery}\n\n## Replanning Guidelines\n- Prioritize topics with low mastery (< 40%) — they need the most attention\n- Topics with mastery > 80% can be reviewed less frequently (spaced repetition)\n- If many days are missed and time is tight, consider dropping review of strong\n  topics entirely to focus on weak ones\n- Include a mix of action types: quiz, explain, review, worked_example\n- Assign higher priority (1-10) to more urgent topics\n- Plan for at most 7 days ahead (or fewer if exam is closer)\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "reasoning": "2-3 sentences explaining the replanning strategy",\n    "trade_offs": "What was deprioritized and why",\n    "entries": [\n        {{\n            "day_offset": 0,\n            "topic_id": <int>,\n            "topic_name": "<name>",\n            "action_type": "quiz|explain|review|worked_example|mock_paper",\n            "priority": <1-10>,\n            "notes": "Brief reasoning for this entry"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}'
EXTRACT_TOPICS_PROMPT = 'Extract the main academic topics and subtopics from this study material.\n\n## Document Text\n{document_text}\n\n## Instructions\n- Identify distinct, teachable topics (not too broad, not too narrow)\n- Each topic should be something you could write quiz questions about\n- Include subtopics where appropriate\n- Order them logically (prerequisites first)\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON array of strings:\n["Topic 1", "Topic 2", "Topic 3", ...]'
GENERATE_MOCK_PROMPT = 'Generate a comprehensive mock exam paper.\n\n**Subject:** {subject_name}\n**Total Questions:** {total_questions}\n**Topics and Mastery (lower = weaker, weight questions toward weaker topics):**\n{topic_mastery}\n\n## Requirements\n- Weight ~60% of questions toward topics with mastery < 50%\n- Include a mix of easy (20%), medium (50%), and hard (30%) questions\n- Mix question types: MCQ and short-answer\n- Each question should have marks assigned (1-5 based on difficulty)\n- Make it feel like a real exam paper\n\n## Output Format\nRespond with ONLY a valid JSON object:\n{{\n    "title": "Mock Exam — {subject_name}",\n    "subject": "{subject_name}",\n    "total_marks": <sum of all marks>,\n    "duration_minutes": <recommended time>,\n    "questions": [\n        {{\n            "number": 1,\n            "question": "Question text",\n            "question_type": "mcq|short_answer",\n            "options": ["A", "B", "C", "D"] or null,\n            "correct_answer": "The answer",\n            "marks": <1-5>,\n            "topic_name": "Which topic this tests",\n            "difficulty": "easy|medium|hard"\n        }}\n    ],\n    "focus_areas": ["Weak topic 1", "Weak topic 2"]\n}}'